      "id": 392505,
      "username": "kaimoeller",
      "name": "Kai-Uwe Moeller",
      "created_at": "2024-02-04T23:50:55.718Z",
      "cooked": "<p>I am currently evaluating ErpNext for a customer. For this customer it is important to follow purchased and manufactured goods to the installation site of the customer, identified by their serial no. A customer can have multiple installation sites.</p>\n<p>So far I have managed to route serials from the purchase order through the delivery note. By FIFO, delivery note will pick serials out of the purchased pool which is fine. Of course I need to print the serials on the delivery note doc and/or the pick list.</p>\n<p>But I do not get the serials automatically into the installation note when I reference delivery note items. Even worse, when I want to submit the installation note, the system complains that the item is missing a serial. So I had to create a new Serial/Batch bundle or something but that’s not the purpose I think as I have my itemized serial already</p>\n<p>My question:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Am I just missing something?</li>\n<li>Can or has that to be customized in the code and if so, where?</li>\n</ul>\n<p>At the end I need a digest that shows me a customer’s site (address) with all installed items and their serial. But that should be doable by a report.</p>\n<p>Thanks<br>\nThis is my very first post here, I hope it’s okay</p>",
